    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f9ba7203-2570-51cf-ab13-922610835a8c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $4-8\\sin^2\\left(110^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Factor out $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&4-8\\sin^2\\left(110^\\circ\\right)\\\\&\\qquad=4\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(110^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=110^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(110^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 110^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(220^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(110^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=4\\cos\\left(220^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
